Wildlife Network Studio: BatDetect2 component (crates/batdetect2)

This folder contains a Rust translation of the processing in BatDetect2, by Oisin Mac Aodha, Santiago Martinez
Balvanera and contributors: https://github.com/macaodha/batdetect2

It reproduces BatDetect2's published method (spectrogram, PCEN, resizing, running the network and decoding calls)
so that Studio's results match BatDetect2's. Because it is a direct translation of their code, this folder is
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0), the same
licence as BatDetect2, at the request of BatDetect2's authors (Oisin Mac Aodha, email of 9 November 2026). See LICENSE.
It may not be used for commercial purposes. The rest of Wildlife Network Studio is licensed under Apache-2.0.

What is in this folder:
- src/lib.rs: BatDetect2's spectrogram, network run and call decoding.
- src/resample.rs: scipy.signal.resample_poly as BatDetect2 calls it. The resampling method is from SciPy
  (https://scipy.org, BSD 3-Clause licence).
- python/export_model.py: turns the official BatDetect2 UK checkpoint into the ONNX file Studio loads. It installs
  nothing itself; it uses the official batdetect2 Python package from PyPI.
- python/make_test_fixture.py and tests/fixtures: reference values from BatDetect2's own Python code, used by the tests.

The BatDetect2 model itself is not in this repository and is not hosted by Wildlife Network. It is published only
by its authors, in the batdetect2 package (https://pypi.org/project/batdetect2/ and the GitHub repository above).

